# The compiled orchestrator. Built on demand by _tools/gen/build.sh (and by
# hand with `go build -o bin/site-build ./cmd/site-build`), never versioned —
# §11.4.30 forbids committing a build derivative.
#
# It is BUILT rather than `go run`-ed for a measured reason: `go run` collapses
# every non-zero program exit into 1 and prints "exit status N", which destroys
# this program's three-valued contract. Measured 2026-09-03, same binary, same
# arguments:
#
#   go run ./cmd/site-build -root /tmp -probe   -> rc 1   (wrong)
#   ./bin/site-build        -root /tmp -probe   -> rc 2   (correct: COULD NOT DETERMINE)
#
# A 2 that arrives as a 1 is an UNDETERMINED result reported as a real failure.
/bin/
